For all designs I ask you to make, have them be beautiful, not cookie cutter. Make webpages that are fully featured and worthy for production.

By default, this template supports JSX syntax with Tailwind CSS classes, React hooks, and Lucide React for icons. Do not install other packages for UI themes, icons, etc unless absolutely necessary or I request them.

Use icons from lucide-react for logos.

bolt_knowledge:
  id: sanctuary_intra_comparative_study
  version: 1.0
  title: "Sanctuary Intra-Comparative Study Interactive Website"
  source: "jesusinhissanctuary.org"
  summary: >
    A dynamic, research-based digital platform exploring the biblical sanctuary doctrine
    through Seventh-day Adventist theology, integrating 3D visualization, comparative study,
    and immersive learning experiences for global audiences.

  objectives:
    - Deliver accurate, immersive, and biblically faithful education on the sanctuary doctrine.
    - Facilitate comparative analysis across traditions and historical contexts.
    - Provide scholarly tools and interactive visuals for deep theological study.
    - Foster respectful dialogue through moderated academic discussion.
    - Create a lasting, sustainable, and expanding theological knowledge platform.

  audience:
    - Adventist members
    - Bible students and educators
    - Scholars and theologians
    - Comparative religion researchers
    - Digital learners seeking visual biblical understanding

  design_core:
    homepage_vision: >
      The homepage acts as a gateway to exploration, featuring interactive 3D models of the
      tabernacle, Solomon’s temple, Zerubbabel’s temple, Herod’s temple, and the heavenly sanctuary.
      Users can zoom, pan, rotate, and tour each space in detail.

    3d_models:
      technologies:
        - WebGL 2.0
        - Babylon.js (premium engine)
        - PBR materials and volumetric lighting
        - Progressive asset loading
      features:
        - Contextual hotspots and access points
        - Cinematic camera navigation
        - Historical and symbolic overlays
        - Interactive light and shadow simulation
      models:
        - Wilderness Tabernacle
        - Solomon’s Temple
        - Zerubbabel’s Temple
        - Herod’s Temple
        - Heavenly Sanctuary (symbolic and prophetic)
      visualization_modes:
        - Guided Tours
        - Component Isolation / X-Ray view
        - Exploded View Mode
        - Material Analysis
        - Comparative Transitions

  compare_mode:
    description: >
      Side-by-side sanctuary analysis mode enabling synchronized navigation, structural comparison,
      and symbolic overlays.
    features:
      - Synchronized navigation across multiple sanctuaries
      - Annotated overlays and tooltips
      - Color-coded material or spatial contrasts
      - Exportable comparison charts for educators and researchers

  scripture_navigator:
    description: >
      Links Scripture directly to 3D model components for contextualized study.
    capabilities:
      - Highlighting of sanctuary sections by biblical reference
      - Cross-references, commentary, and language tools
      - Toggle between Bible translations (KJV, ESV, NIV)
      - Integration of Greek/Hebrew lexical data

  symbolism_mode:
    description: >
      Furnishing-based theological exploration presenting symbolic meaning through multiple traditions.
    contexts:
      - Judaism (rabbinic interpretation)
      - Christianity (Christological types)
      - Seventh-day Adventist theology (prophetic and soteriological context)
    includes:
      - Scripture cross-references
      - Ellen G. White commentary
      - Modern Adventist scholarly sources
      - Toggle by religious tradition for comparison

  historical_timeline:
    description: >
      Interactive chronological timeline showing the evolution of sanctuary theology and its fulfillment in Christ.
    features:
      - Scrollable time slider with sanctuary-to-Christ typology
      - 24-step Aaronic type vs. Christ anti-type placeholders
      - Embedded scripture, video, and article links
      - Integration of historical, prophetic, and doctrinal events

  multimedia_learning:
    animated_videos:
      duration: "1–5 minutes each"
      languages: [Spanish, Portuguese, Russian, Chinese, French, Arabic]
      features:
        - Voice narration and subtitles
        - Scriptural cross-references
        - Accessibility-focused transcripts
    heavenly_portal:
      description: >
        Immersive WebGL simulation of the Heavenly Sanctuary experience
        (Daniel 7, Revelation 4–5, Hebrews 9).
      features:
        - Progressive journey from earthly to heavenly courts
        - Celestial visual and audio atmosphere
        - Scripture overlays and ambient music

  learning_modules:
    investigative_judgment:
      focus: "Doctrine of the investigative judgment and sanctuary cleansing"
      tools:
        - Animated flowcharts (Daniel 8:14 → 1844 → present)
        - Clickable cross-references
        - Historical context of the Millerite movement
        - Reflection quizzes
    digital_library:
      content:
        - Peer-reviewed academic papers
        - Classic Adventist texts (ML Andreasen, EG White, Haskell, Hardinge, etc.)
        - PDF downloads with citation support
      search_filters:
        - Keyword
        - Author
        - Scripture reference
        - Tradition
    discussion_forums:
      security:
        - OAuth login
        - Two-factor authentication
        - AI-assisted content moderation
      structure:
        - Thematic study groups
        - Global multilingual participation
        - Notification and reply tracking
    personalized_learning:
      user_profiles:
        - Save learning progress and bookmarks
        - Track engagement analytics
        - Achievement badges and certificates
        - Personalized content suggestions

  outreach_features:
    myth_vs_fact:
      description: "Quiz-based learning to clarify sanctuary misconceptions"
      audience: ["Individuals", "Study groups", "Educators"]
    educator_resources:
      includes:
        - Lesson plans
        - Discussion activities
        - Presentation slides
        - Licensing for non-commercial educational use
    companion_media:
      title: "Sanctuary Insights"
      format: ["Podcast", "Video series"]
      content:
        - Weekly interviews and theological discussions
        - Transcripts and study guides
        - Distribution via 3ABN, Hope Channel, YouTube

  technical_framework:
    mobile_and_pwa:
      features:
        - Full responsive design
        - Offline Progressive Web App (PWA) mode
        - Optimized 3D rendering for mobile devices
        - Gesture and touch support
    seo_discoverability:
      strategies:
        - Schema.org markup for scripture and resources
        - SEO metadata optimization
        - Multilingual support
        - Internal cross-linking
    academic_partnerships:
      institutions:
        - Andrews University Theological Seminary
        - Loma Linda University
        - Adventist Graduate School
      contributions:
        - Peer review and theological oversight
        - Faculty advisory content
        - Institutional endorsements

  sustainability_plan:
    continuous_improvement:
      - User rating and feedback systems
      - Iterative UX testing
      - Analytics-driven updates
    multilingual_expansion:
      next_languages: [Indonesian, Hindi, Swahili, French]
      strategy: "Volunteer translation via global Adventist network"
    long_term_vision:
      - Donation and volunteer contributor model
      - Cloud-based data backup (AWS/Google Cloud)
      - Editorial and technical governance boards

  conclusion: >
    The Sanctuary Intra-Comparative Study Interactive Website merges biblical accuracy, theological
    scholarship, and immersive 3D technology into a transformative learning experience. By connecting
    ancient sanctuary symbolism with modern interactivity, it provides a comprehensive platform for
    global Adventist education, digital discipleship, and scholarly engagement.